From 1ca64cea3da0d3121a37b47801f3bd87451312e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 23:26:24 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] ANDROID: add aggressive performance profile for arm64 GKI

Add a compile-time Android profile for latency-first custom kernels.
Raise schedutil DVFS headroom and I/O wake boost, cap its initial
transition rate limit, and install zram-oriented reclaim defaults.

Add a separate emergency-only generic thermal mode. It bypasses
active/passive governor actions while preserving HOT/CRITICAL handling
and emergency poweroff. Firmware, hardware, vendor drivers, and directly
polling thermal services remain outside this bypass.

Enable the profile in arm64 gki_defconfig together with a 1000 Hz tick,
non-lazy RCU callbacks, LZ4 zram, and optional zram writeback support.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
